   "source": [
    "## 1) Matrices & Operations\n",
    "\n",
    "We review basic operations (addition, multiplication, transpose, determinant, inverse) and relate them to ML tasks such as feature transforms.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "15fce7c8",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Define two small matrices and perform basic ops\n",
    "A = np.array([[1, 3],\n",
    "              [2, 4]], dtype=float)\n",
    "\n",
    "B = np.array([[2, 1],\n",
    "              [1, 3]], dtype=float)\n",
    "\n",
    "C = np.array([[2, 3],\n",
    "              [1, 4]], dtype=float)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"A =\\n\", A)\n",
    "print(\"B =\\n\", B)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nAddition: A + B =\\n\", A + B)\n",
    "print(\"\\nMatrix product: A @ B =\\n\", A @ B)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"\\nTranspose: A.T =\\n\", A.T)\n",
    "\n",
    "detC = np.linalg.det(C)\n",
    "print(\"\\nDeterminant det(C) =\", round(detC, 3))\n",
    "\n",
    "if abs(detC) > 1e-12:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nInverse of C =\\n\", np.linalg.inv(C))\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"\\nC is singular; inverse does not exist.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "acac96d9",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2) Vector Spaces & Linear Independence\n",
    "\n",
    "A simple way to **test linear independence** numerically is to form a matrix with the vectors as columns and check its rank.\n",
    "- If rank equals the number of vectors, they are linearly independent.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "1113248e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# 2D example: two vectors\n",
    "v1 = np.array([1, 0.0])\n",
    "v2 = np.array([0, 1.0])\n",
    "\n",
    "M = np.column_stack([v1, v2])\n",
    "rank = np.linalg.matrix_rank(M)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Vectors as columns:\\n\", M)\n",
    "print(\"Rank =\", rank, \" — independent?\" , rank == M.shape[1])"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9e3f5352",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3) Eigenvalues & Eigenvectors\n",
    "\n",
    "We compute eigenvalues/eigenvectors and show how a linear transform stretches/rotates the plane. Try changing the matrix `A`.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "3d50f673",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Choose a 2x2 matrix for geometric intuition\n",
    "A = np.array([[4.0, 1.0],\n",
    "              [2.0, 3.0]])\n",
    "\n",
    "vals, vecs = np.linalg.eig(A)\n",
    "print(\"Eigenvalues:\\n\", vals)\n",
    "print(\"\\nEigenvectors (columns):\\n\", vecs)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Visualize the transform of the unit vectors and a grid\n",
    "def plot_linear_transform(A, lim=3.0, step=1.0):\n",
    "    # make a grid of points and transform them\n",
    "    xs = np.arange(-lim, lim+1e-9, step)\n",
    "    ys = np.arange(-lim, lim+1e-9, step)\n",
    "    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 6))\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Plot original grid\n",
    "    for x in xs:\n",
    "        ax.plot([x]*len(ys), ys, linewidth=0.6)\n",
    "    for y in ys:\n",
    "        ax.plot(xs, [y]*len(xs), linewidth=0.6)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Plot transformed grid\n",
    "    for x in xs:\n",
    "        pts = np.vstack([np.full_like(ys, x), ys])\n",
    "        tpts = A @ pts\n",
    "        ax.plot(tpts[0], tpts[1], linewidth=0.6)\n",
    "    for y in ys:\n",
    "        pts = np.vstack([xs, np.full_like(xs, y)])\n",
    "        tpts = A @ pts\n",
    "        ax.plot(tpts[0], tpts[1], linewidth=0.6)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Show how unit vectors transform\n",
    "    e1 = np.array([1.0, 0.0])\n",
    "    e2 = np.array([0.0, 1.0])\n",
    "    Ae1 = A @ e1\n",
    "    Ae2 = A @ e2\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.arrow(0, 0, e1[0], e1[1], head_width=0.1, length_includes_head=True)\n",
    "    ax.arrow(0, 0, e2[0], e2[1], head_width=0.1, length_includes_head=True)\n",
    "    ax.arrow(0, 0, Ae1[0], Ae1[1], head_width=0.1, length_includes_head=True)\n",
    "    ax.arrow(0, 0, Ae2[0], Ae2[1], head_width=0.1, length_includes_head=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "    ax.set_aspect('equal', 'box')\n",
    "    ax.set_xlim(-lim*2, lim*2)\n",
    "    ax.set_ylim(-lim*2, lim*2)\n",
    "    ax.set_title(\"Original grid (thin) and Transformed grid (thin)\\nArrows: e1,e2 and A e1, A e2\")\n",
    "    ax.set_xlabel(\"x\")\n",
    "    ax.set_ylabel(\"y\")\n",
    "    plt.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_linear_transform(A)"
   ]
  },
